chapter AFP

session Datalog_Graph = Datalog_Certification +
  description \<open>Datalog-to-graph (Path 2 of the certificate foundedness story): convert a datalog
    certificate to the graph library's \<open>dgraph\<close> support graph and discharge the foundedness
    obligation \<open>dl_founded\<close> from acyclicity of that graph (\<open>Datalog_To_Graph\<close>), then discharge
    acyclicity itself executably with the verified whole-graph directed-cycle sweep
    (\<open>Datalog_Cycle_DFS\<close>). The graph library (Directed_Set_Graphs) is pulled in HERE and nowhere
    else, so its imperative/Separation_Logic stack never meets the AFP Collections/ODE tower of the
    PDDL branch.

    The graph-theoretic ingredients themselves (the topological-numbering characterisation of
    acyclicity, and the directed-cycle sweep with its skeleton) carry no datalog and live upstream
    in the graph library's \<open>Directed_Cycle_DFS\<close> session; this session only instantiates them at
    the certificate's support graph.

    \<^bold>\<open>Which level of the sweep is used where.\<close> \<open>Directed_Cycle_DFS\<close> develops the sweep as a chain of
    refinements. \<open>Datalog_Cycle_DFS\<close> instantiates \<^emph>\<open>level 0\<close> (\<open>DFS_DirCycle_Linear\<close>), the
    reference implementation: it is the simplest to instantiate and it is what the correctness
    argument is stated against. \<open>Datalog_Cycle_DFS_Code\<close> then re-instantiates the \<^emph>\<open>most
    refined\<close> level and inherits that correctness through the chain's equivalence theorems, so the
    code that actually runs pays for none of the set differences while nothing downstream has to
    be reproved. Keeping the two apart is deliberate: the specification instance stays stable as
    further refinements are added below it.\<close>
  options [timeout = 600]
  sessions
    "Directed_Set_Graphs"
    "Directed_Cycle_DFS"
  theories
    Datalog_To_Graph
    Datalog_Cycle_DFS
    Datalog_Cycle_DFS_Code
    Datalog_Certificate_Index
